{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"acidotic-knowing-kestrel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# DC sub-task parent sync is UNIMPLEMENTED — two live cells have never passed in any harness run\n\n## Status\n\nFiled under epic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb] because it BLOCKS the epic: the epic's goal is working\nJira DC functionality without bugs, and two live DC cells fail on every run. Operator ruling\n(2026-08-04): **resolve the failures; do NOT remove or `xfail` the failing tests.**\n\n## Evidence — never passed, measured across 12 consecutive harness runs\n\nPer-cell failing sets were extracted from every `Live External Integration` harness job from\n`30834117797` (08-03 16:52) through `30951453979` (08-04 21:14). Both cells below appear in the\nFAILED set of **all 12**:\n\n    test_inbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips     12/12 runs FAILED\n    test_outbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips    12/12 runs FAILED\n\n**This is the \"never passed\" case, NOT a regression** — so there is no bisect to run and no commit to\nrevert; the work was diagnosed and never done. The distinction was checked because it changes the\nremedy, and the surrounding data proves the harness CAN detect fixes: it improved 6 -> 3 failures over\nthe same window, with `inbound_delete_link_round_trips`,\n`outbound_create_stamps_both_provenance_markers`, `set_parent_declines_the_epic_case_loudly`,\n`outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link`, `inbound_clear_parent_round_trips` and\n`test_the_instance_label_ceiling_measured_at_254_and_255` each dropping out at an identifiable run.\nThese two never dropped out.\n\nDiagnosed but not fixed by [rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda] (closed) and\n[rebar:39c1-2a32-b564-4b4b] (closed). Both closed with a `completion-verifier: PASS` on their\nDIAGNOSIS; neither delivered a behaviour change that made a cell pass.\n\n## Mechanism — two INDEPENDENT gaps, one platform and one rebar-side\n\n**1. Platform (1a9f): DC accepts `PUT fields.parent` on a sub-task and silently ignores it.**\nRe-confirmed LIVE today, not merely inherited from the capability map: run `30951453979` asked for\n`RBJREXN-2`, Jira accepted the write, and a fresh read still reported `RBJREXN-1`. Capability map\nreq-0056 (HTTP 204) / req-0058 (read-back unchanged) agree. Re-asserting this mattered because this\nsame epic RETRACTED the map's label-ceiling entry after the live cell contradicted it — a recorded\nmeasurement is not settled until re-measured. This one holds.\n\nClearing is separately impossible on a sub-task: `{\"fields\":{\"parent\":null}}` -> 400,\n`{\"update\":{\"parent\":[{\"set\":null}]}}` -> 400, and sub-task `editmeta` exposes NO `parent` field at\nall (req-0054/0055/0057, [rebar:37e7-d751-0042-4b94]).\n\n**2. rebar-side (39c1): the outbound parent-set can never be EMITTED on DC.** The apply side accepts\nonly a SUB-TASK child (`adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py` `set_parent`, checks\n`fields.issuetype.subtask`, raises `NotImplementedError` for a non-sub-task naming the Epic Link\nreason). The emit side omits the parent field entirely for any parent whose local `ticket_type` is not\n`epic` (`outbound_field_diff._resolve_local_parent:136-139`, bug 8b25's hierarchy guard). A DC\nsub-task's parent is a STANDARD issue, which imports as local type `task`. **The two gates are\ndisjoint, so no reconcile pass can carry a parent-set on DC at all.** This half is entirely inside\nrebar and is fixable without any platform capability.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Establish by LIVE measurement whether ANY supported DC mechanism can move a sub-task's parent\n      (`fields.parent` is measured accept-and-ignore). Record the answer as data with the run id —\n      including the negative case, which is a legitimate outcome here\n- [ ] 39c1's emit-side gap is CLOSED: a reconcile pass on DC can emit a parent mutation for the\n      child/parent shapes DC actually accepts, so the emit and apply gates are no longer disjoint\n- [ ] rebar never issues a write DC is measured to accept-and-ignore: the unsupported case fails\n      LOUDLY (raise + bridge alert naming the reason), never a silent no-op that reports success\n- [ ] `test_inbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips` and\n      `test_outbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips` both PASS in a harness run, asserting the\n      user-visible outcome (the child ends up under the intended parent). If AC1 establishes that\n      `fields.parent` cannot work on a sub-task, the cells are RE-HOMED to the mechanism DC does\n      support — the same operator-endorsed move as b9b8 (Row 14) and [rebar:4b9e-bcad-456a-4233] —\n      and the re-homed oracle asserts that same outcome. Re-homing is NOT weakening: an oracle for an\n      operation the platform cannot perform is a wrong oracle, but the hierarchy outcome must still\n      be asserted end to end\n- [ ] no cell is deleted, skipped, or `xfail`ed to reach green (operator ruling)\n- [ ] `docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` records the outcome with the run id\n\n## Testing\n\n    # the live DC harness (workflow_dispatch), which is the only place these cells run\n    gh workflow run \"Live External Integration\" --ref main\n    pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler -q","id":"9f26-66c2-14af-4223","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC sub-task parent sync is unimplemented: two live cells have never passed in any harness run"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785881433398491001,"uuid":"20f89011-05b8-4acf-b36e-134c21b5c5d6"}